cb1b0d33e6a"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 880x550 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Appointment Outcome Analysis**\n","\n","Appointment outcomes show that No-Show is the most common outcome, accounting for 2,423 appointments or 48.46% of all appointments. A total of 2,314 appointments were attended, representing an attendance rate of 46.28%, while 263 appointments were cancelled, representing 5.26%.\n","The high no-show rate is a major operational concern because almost half of scheduled appointments did not result in patient attendance. This suggests that improving appointment adherence should be a major priority for HealthConnect.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"2mofUUc-SBbB"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["pd.crosstab(\n","clean_df['reminder_sent'],\n","clean_df['outcome_clean']\n",").plot(\n","kind='bar',\n","figsize=(8,5)\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Reminder Sent vs Appointment Outcome')\n","plt.xlabel('Reminder Sent')\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Appointments')\n","plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":421},"id":"wNoFhtEB40Pj","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790254678390,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":42,"user":{"displayName":"Pamela Ferdinand","userId":"05913115544278263948"}},"outputId":"6ea847bf-adb7-4ed5-d1ae-d6786df69961"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 880x550 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Reminder Effectiveness**\n","\n","Appointments without reminders had a 51.39% no-show rate, compared with 47.36% among appointments where a reminder was sent.\n","This represents a reduction of approximately 4.03 percentage points in the no-show rate when reminders were sent. Although reminders do not eliminate no-shows, the result suggests that reminder communication may contribute to improved appointment attendance.\n","However, the relationship should be interpreted as an association rather than proof that reminders directly caused the improvement.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"g7zpd5uWZFuP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Reminder Channel Analysis**\n","\n","Among appointments where a reminder was sent, SMS had the lowest no-show rate at 45.75%, followed by Email at 48.41% and WhatsApp at 49.77%.\n","SMS also had the highest attendance rate at 49.60%. This suggests that SMS may be the most effective reminder channel in this dataset.\n","However, channel effectiveness should be evaluated cautiously because patients may not have been randomly assigned to reminder channels.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"jKH6aqGbZN6z"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["pd.crosstab(\n","clean_df['lead_time_group'],\n","clean_df['outcome_clean']\n",").plot(\n","kind='bar',\n","figsize=(10,6)\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Appointment Outcomes by Booking Lead Time')\n","plt.xlabel('Booking Lead Time')\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Appointments')\n","plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":406},"id":"Ft6z6nkC5Hb2","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790254678455,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":31,"user":{"displayName":"Pamela Ferdinand","userId":"05913115544278263948"}},"outputId":"281b1297-cfea-4f88-d174-9dd81cc7c76d"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1100x660 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Booking Lead Time Analysis**\n","\n","A strong relationship was observed between booking lead time and appointment attendance.\n","Appointments booked 0–7 days in advance had a 27.81% no-show rate, compared with 40.21% for appointments booked 8–30 days in advance. Appointments booked 31–60 days in advance had the highest no-show rate at 60.49%.\n","This suggests that longer waiting periods between booking and appointment dates may increase the likelihood of patients missing appointments. Shorter booking windows and additional reminders closer to the appointment date may therefore help reduce no-shows.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"jacwQmTvZeAe"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A strong relationship was observed between booking lead time and appointment attendance.\n","Appointments booked 0–7 days in advance had a 27.81% no-show rate, compared with 40.21% for appointments booked 8–30 days in advance. Appointments booked 31–60 days in advance had the highest no-show rate at 60.49%.\n","This suggests that longer waiting periods between booking and appointment dates may increase the likelihood of patients missing appointments. Shorter booking windows and additional reminders closer to the appointment date may therefore help reduce no-shows.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"KC3P6yZZRjqk"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["pd.crosstab(\n","clean_df['previous_no_shows'],\n","clean_df['outcome_clean']\n",").plot(\n","kind='bar',\n","figsize=(10,6)\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Appointment Outcomes by Previous No-Shows')\n","plt.xlabel('Previous No-Shows')\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Appointments')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":405},"id":"A7uDBmiv5PwT","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790254678491,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":38,"user":{"displayName":"Pamela Ferdinand","userId":"05913115544278263948"}},"outputId":"2f427560-ec4e-4dfe-a0ce-517ed863eef3"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1100x660 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Previous No-Show Behaviour**\n","\n","Previous no-show behaviour is one of the strongest patterns identified in the analysis.\n","Patients with no previous no-shows had a 43.51% current no-show rate. This increased to 53.49% among patients with one previous no-show, 59.36% among those with two, and 67.95% among those with three previous no-shows.\n","This indicates that previous appointment behaviour can be a useful indicator of future appointment adherence. HealthConnect could therefore use previous no-show history to identify high-risk appointments and provide additional reminders or follow-up.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"WmfqCEYCZwbm"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["pd.crosstab(\n","clean_df['age_group'],\n","clean_df['outcome_clean']\n",").plot(\n","kind='bar',\n","figsize=(10,6)\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Appointment Outcomes by Age Group')\n","plt.xlabel('Age Group')\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Appointments')\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":405},"id":"kA3DwTCB5aKf","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790254678540,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":48,"user":{"displayName":"Pamela Ferdinand","userId":"05913115544278263948"}},"outputId":"1386f0e6-fd52-4491-9397-25a15bbd702c"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1100x660 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Age Group Analysis**\n","\n","No-show rates were relatively similar across most age groups. The highest no-show rate was observed among patients aged 25–34 at 50.70%, followed closely by the 55–64 group at 50.75% and the 18–24 group at 50.18%.\n","Patients aged 65 and above recorded the lowest no-show rate at 45.12% and the highest attendance rate at 48.75%.\n","Overall, age appears to have a weaker relationship with appointment attendance than factors such as previous no-show behaviour and booking lead time.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"PfPX5aTCZ2pf"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["pd.crosstab(\n","clean_df['appointment_type'],\n","clean_df['outcome_clean']\n",").plot(\n","kind='bar',\n","figsize=(10,6)\n",")\n","\n