      \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"cancelled\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0.6766584564362339,\n        \"min\": 4.38,\n        \"max\": 6.0,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 4,\n        \"samples\": [\n          5.42,\n          6.0,\n          4.38\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"no-show\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 2.1069488207674456,\n        \"min\": 46.64,\n        \"max\": 51.23,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 4,\n        \"samples\": [\n          51.23,\n          47.44,\n          49.75\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}},"metadata":{},"execution_count":58}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Key Performance Indicators**\n","\n","The analysis produced the following key performance indicators:\n","• Total Appointments: 5,000\n","\n","• Total Patients: 1,696\n","\n","• Total No-Shows: 2,423\n","\n","• No-Show Rate: 48.46%\n","\n","• Total Attended: 2,314\n","\n","• Attendance Rate: 46.28%\n","\n","• Total Cancelled: 263\n","\n","• Cancellation Rate: 5.26%\n","\n","These KPIs provide a concise view of appointment utilisation and patient attendance and can serve as baseline measures for future monitoring.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"pYTinomSa4ub"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Visualization Summary**\n","\n","The visualizations reinforce the major patterns identified during the exploratory analysis. The appointment outcome chart highlights the high proportion of no-shows, while the reminder analysis shows a lower no-show rate among appointments where reminders were sent.\n","The booking lead-time analysis shows that longer booking periods are associated with higher no-show rates. The previous no-show analysis also demonstrates a clear increase in current no-shows as previous no-show history increases.\n","Age-group and appointment-type visualizations show smaller differences across categories compared with booking behaviour and previous attendance history.\n","Overall, the visual analysis suggests that patient appointment history, previous no-shows, booking lead time and reminder activity are important areas for operational attention.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"ElvmjQtAbN-n"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Business Insights**\n","\n","1. No-shows are the major operational challenge. HealthConnect recorded 2,423 no-shows out of 5,000 appointments, resulting in a high no-show rate of 48.46%. Almost half of scheduled appointments therefore did not result in attendance.\n","2. Reminder communication is associated with improved attendance. Appointments with reminders had a no-show rate of 47.36%, compared with 51.39% for appointments without reminders.\n","3. SMS appears to be the strongest reminder channel. SMS recorded the lowest no-show rate among the available reminder channels at 45.75%, compared with 48.41% for Email and 49.77% for WhatsApp.\n","4. Previous no-show behaviour is a strong indicator of future risk. The no-show rate increased from 43.51% among patients with no previous no-shows to 67.95% among patients with three previous no-shows.\n","5. Longer booking lead times are associated with higher no-show rates. The no-show rate increased from 27.81% for appointments booked 0–7 days ahead to 60.49% for appointments booked 31–60 days ahead.\n","6. Age has a relatively weak relationship with attendance. No-show rates were close to 50% across most age groups.\n","7. Follow-up appointments require additional attention. Follow-up appointments recorded the highest no-show rate among appointment types at 51.23%.\n","8. The dataset is generally structurally reliable. No duplicate records were identified and no major logical inconsistencies were detected during the initial quality checks.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"TZWwLrgkbV-b"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["** Limitations**\n","1. Observational data: The analysis identifies associations between variables and appointment outcomes but cannot establish causation.\n","2. Missing values: The dataset contains missing values, particularly in reminder_channel, distance_to_clinic_km and waiting_time_minutes. These missing observations may affect analyses involving these variables.\n","3. Unequal group sizes: Some categories, particularly patients with four or five previous no-shows, may contain relatively few observations. Therefore, very high percentages in these groups should be interpreted cautiously.\n","4. Limited explanatory variables: The dataset does not contain some potentially important factors such as patient income, transportation availability, employment schedule, reason for missing an appointment, health status or socioeconomic conditions.\n","5. Reminder selection bias: Patients receiving different reminder channels may have been selected based on factors not captured in the dataset. Therefore, SMS having a lower no-show rate does not necessarily mean SMS directly causes better attendance.\n","6. No predictive model was developed in this analysis: The current analysis focuses on exploratory data analysis and KPI development. It does not provide an individual-level prediction of which patient will miss an appointment.\n","7. Historical dataset: The findings describe the available HealthConnect records and may not necessarily represent future appointment behaviour without ongoing monitoring.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"jd3BoYkGbnP5"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["** Recommendations**\n","1. Strengthen appointment reminder systems. HealthConnect should maintain and improve reminder communication because appointments with reminders showed a lower no-show rate than appointments without reminders.\n","2. Prioritize high-risk patients. Patients with previous no-shows should receive additional reminders or follow-up communication because previous no-show behaviour is strongly associated with future no-shows.\n","3. Increase reminders for appointments booked far in advance. Appointments scheduled 31–60 days ahead had a 60.49% no-show rate. HealthConnect should consider additional reminders at booking, one week before the appointment and shortly before the appointment date.\n","4. Test SMS as the primary reminder channel. SMS recorded the lowest no-show rate among the reminder channels analysed. HealthConnect could prioritize SMS while continuing to monitor WhatsApp and Email performance.\n","5. Review follow-up appointment processes. Follow-up appointments recorded the highest no-show rate among appointment types. The clinic should consider additional confirmation messages and easier appointment rescheduling for follow-up patients.\n","6. Introduce appointment confirmation and rescheduling. Patients could be given a simple option to confirm, cancel or reschedule appointments before the appointment date. This may help convert some potential no-shows into cancellations or rescheduled visits.\n","7. Monitor waiting time. Although waiting time was not the main focus of this analysis, HealthConnect should continue monitoring it because long waiting times can affect patient satisfaction and future attendance.\n","8. Build a no-show risk monitoring system. The variables identified in this analysis, particularly previous no-shows and booking lead time, can be used as inputs for a future predictive model that identifies appointments at high risk of no-show.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"67ekbvaocLaT"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Conclusion**\n","\n","Overall, the Week 5 analysis identified a high appointment no-show rate and several important factors associated with attendance behaviour. Previous no-show history and booking lead time showed the clearest relationships with current appointment outcomes, while reminder activity was associated with a modest reduction in no-shows. These findings provide a strong basis for targeted patient engagement and for developing a predictive no-show model in Week 6.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"64ManHCJdGVY"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**HealthConnect Week 6**\n","\n","Advanced Analytics & Decision Support Builds on Week 5's cleaned dataset (clean_df).\n","\n","**Focus:** validate findings, test interactions, integrate with Data Science.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"_mP6ENqQGDf6"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["clean_df['previous_no_shows'].value_counts().sort_index()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":303},"id":"LULjBrCMIip8","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790254679253,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":230,"user":{"displayName":"Pamela Ferdinand","userId":"05913115544278263948"}},"outputId":"cc8b0519-baee-4439-ca89-d03f1c164275"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["previous_no_shows\n","0    2921\n","1    1548\n","2     438\n","3      78\n","4      12\n","5       3\n","Name: count, dtype: int64"],"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>count</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>previous_no_shows</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>0</th>\n","      <td>2921</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>1</th>\n","      <td>1548</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>2</th>\n","      <td>438</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>3</th>\n","      <td>78</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>4</th>\n","      <td>12</td>\n","    </tr>\n